   "subject": "Unconditional confidence intervals in GLM models",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Hello everyone,<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"> </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">First, I hope this question\r\nisn&#39;t off topic.<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"> </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">I have a database with 62\r\nsites and 6 covariates, my data are binomial (0,1). So, I did 7 GLM models and\r\nalso I calculated the model averaging of beta estimates in R with the\r\nAICcmodavg package. <u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">My models: <u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Cand.models &lt;- list( )<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Cand.models[[1]]&lt;-glm(Estado~1,family=binomial(link=&quot;logit&quot;),\r\nna.action=na.pass)                            \r\n<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Cand.models[[2]]&lt;-glm(Estado~Biomasa\r\n+Rios+as.factor(Habitat), family=binomial(link=&quot;logit&quot;),\r\nna.action=na.pass)<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Cand.models[[3]]&lt;-glm(Estado~Biomasa\r\n+Elevacion, family=binomial(link=&quot;logit&quot;), na.action=na.pass)<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Cand.models[[4]]&lt;-glm(Estado~Cabmun+as.factor(Habitat),\r\nfamily=binomial(link=&quot;logit&quot;), na.action=na.pass)<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Cand.models[[5]]&lt;-glm(Estado~Rios\r\n+Elevacion+Cabmun, family=binomial(link=&quot;logit&quot;), na.action=na.pass)<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Cand.models[[6]]&lt;-glm(Estado~Biomasa\r\n+Cabmun, family=binomial(link=&quot;logit&quot;), na.action=na.pass)<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Cand.models[[7]]&lt;-glm(Estado~Rios\r\n+Elevacion+as.factor(Habitat), family=binomial(link=&quot;logit&quot;),\r\nna.action=na.pass)<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"> </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">I was wondering how get and\r\nplotting the unconditional confidence intervals for each coefficient\r\nconsidering the model averaging of beta estimates.<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"> </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">I want a graph like this\r\nfor each parameter, but using the model averaging of beta estimates instead of\r\nuse a specific model output (note: for this graphic I used a specific model\r\noutput, specifically, I used the Cand.models[[3]):<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-r3zTmy_fjBU/WM3bxGuiKWI/AAAAAAAACZY/Fzyb0T9TLJcRQNTdY3buGBPDJy6f8a34gCLcB/s1600/Rplot.jpeg\" style=\"clear:left;margin-bottom:1em;float:left;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-r3zTmy_fjBU/WM3bxGuiKWI/AAAAAAAACZY/Fzyb0T9TLJcRQNTdY3buGBPDJy6f8a34gCLcB/s1600/Rplot.jpeg&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792494860918000&amp;usg=AOvVaw13nt2sns7WJVuTHWZEsAur\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-r3zTmy_fjBU/WM3bxGuiKWI/AAAAAAAACZY/Fzyb0T9TLJcRQNTdY3buGBPDJy6f8a34gCLcB/s400/Rplot.jpeg\" border=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"215\"></a><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">If this is possible, how could I do those graphic using the model averaging of beta estimates?</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Thanks for your answers, I really appreciate your help.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">By the way, I attach my database for if it helps</p><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "ZWcSyK5DCAAJ",
   "from": "Daniel Linden",
   "author": "527d9b3ec7deff2d",
   "date": "2017-03-23T13:26:29Z",
   "subject": "Re: Unconditional confidence intervals in GLM models",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Alejandro,<br><br>Model-averaged betas are a bit controversial.  Your analysis would be made much easier to simply condition on your top model and make inferences on covariate effects from that model.  If the covariate effects are weak, there is not much to be gained from plotting them.<br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "6-9ukjyeCQAJ",
   "from": "alejandro...@st.ib.unam.mx",
   "author": "5991381a6385f60d",
   "date": "2017-03-27T23:17:09Z",
   "subject": "Re: Unconditional confidence intervals in GLM models",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hello Daniel,</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks for your response, it makes sense what you suggest.<br></div><div>However, in cases where the model-averaged betas is reasonable, how do I make the script? </div><div>I will really appreciate any help.</div><div><br></div><div>All the best!</div><div><br></div><div>Alejandro</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "efyB1kbLCQAJ",
   "from": "Daniel Linden",
   "author": "527d9b3ec7deff2d",
   "date": "2017-03-28T13:02:31Z",
   "subject": "Re: Unconditional confidence intervals in GLM models",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Sorry, this is actually pretty straightforward with the <span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">modavgPred</span> function:<br><br><span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">newdata &lt;- data.frame(Biomasa = seq(-2,2,0.1),Rios=0,Cabmun=0,Elevacion=0,<br>                      Carreteras = 0, Habitat = factor(&quot;VA&quot;,levels=c(&quot;VA&quot;,&quot;VC&quot;)))<br>pred &lt;- modavgPred(Cand.models,as.character(1:7),newdata)<br>pred$high &lt;- pred$mod.avg.pred + 1.96*pred$<a href=\"http://uncond.se\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://uncond.se&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792494860920000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2RM7WkFSbZoC9ZRs9O_P7a\">uncond.se</a><br>pred$low &lt;- pred$mod.avg.pred - 1.96*pred$<a href=\"http://uncond.se\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://uncond.se&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792494860920000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2RM7WkFSbZoC9ZRs9O_P7a\">uncond.se</a><br><br>plot(newdata$Biomasa,pred$mod.avg.pred,type=&quot;l&quot;,<br>     ylim=c(0,1),ylab=&quot;Probability&quot;,xlab=&quot;Biomasa&quot;)<br>lines(newdata$Biomasa,pred$high,lty=2)<br>lines(newdata$Biomasa,pred$low,lty=2)<br>points(data$Biomasa,data$Estado,pch=16)<br><br></span><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-6_ytCK--Q-4/WNperE3u4YI/AAAAAAAAAfQ/j4GhG0LujSsXH4xxgyFyAqXtYQo2_TDtgCLcB/s1600/biomasa_pumas.png\" style=\"clear:left;margin-bottom:1em;float:left;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-6_ytCK--Q-4/WNperE3u4YI/AAAAAAAAAfQ/j4GhG0LujSsXH4xxgyFyAqXtYQo2_TDtgCLcB/s1600/biomasa_pumas.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792494860920000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3E1Hfxup0NgLszZ520oVN_\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-6_ytCK--Q-4/WNperE3u4YI/AAAAAAAAAfQ/j4GhG0LujSsXH4xxgyFyAqXtYQo2_TDtgCLcB/s400/biomasa_pumas.png\" height=\"308\" border=\"0\" width=\"400\"></a></p></div>"
    ]
   ]
